From af0914a8259dba65d977ac29bb2181219532f3bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PingoLee <eurafael@msn.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:50:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] scheduler: add an experimental fair class for spawned
 tasks

`Threads.@spawn fair=true` marks a root task. Until it first runs, a marked
root waits in FIFO rings, stamped at insert, instead of the priority heaps;
a pop samples two rings and takes the older head. Once it has started, it
and every task it first makes runnable are queued in a second set of the
stock heaps. When both that work and other tasks are waiting, a thread
shares its time equally between the two, so closed-loop clients that spawn
work and wait on it are served in about the order they arrived instead of
being starved by newer work. `fair=false` opts a task out: it, and what it
spawns, are not request work of the marked task that makes it runnable.
Only `:default` tasks are classed, and the keyword is read only for them.
The class is one byte, the last padding byte of the first cache line of
`jl_task_t`. Until something is marked, the scheduler's entry points take
the stock path after one load of a flag.

The keyword is experimental and may change. The time share is a parameter
of `Base.Partr` (`set_fair_weight!`), left internal.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Opus 5.5)
